            <div xml:id="d61-a1">

                <pb facs="0220" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg92"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 327.—Telegrams.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hall to President Cardenas</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 19,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">President <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardenas</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Managua:</hi></p>
                <p>Ever since my return from Nicaragua I have been making efforts, through my
                    Government, to avert a conflict. President Barrios offers me that until my
                    Government is heard from neither Guatemala nor Honduras shall invade Salvador or
                    Nicaragua, if on the part of the two latter the same conduct shall be observed
                    respecting Guatemala and Honduras.</p>
                <p>I hope you will concur with me that this proposal is reasonable and convenient,
                    in which case Nicaragua will undertake no invasion of Honduras. Please
                    answer.</p>
                <closer><signed>HALL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
